{
  "comment": "Real pasted ingredient lines with the one reading both parsers must produce. Read by tests/recipe-parse.test.ts and backend/forkluck/test_recipe_parse_parity.py, so a form fixed on one side cannot drift on the other. Every line here parses with no ingredients in hand, so a `grams` is asserted only where the text itself states the mass: an unmatched name takes no weight from the density chart, a profile each-weight or a bare number. `unit` is the normalized unit, null when the line carried none and nothing matched it; `amount` is the entered quantity, the low end of a written `range`. `kind` marks a heading or a note, `unmeasured` an ingredient the recipe gave no amount for, and both reach no cost in either engine. A skipped line reports its kind and whether the loss affects a price.",
